  "description": "The back of the hand and of the fingers. Between the first and second metacarpals the first web space holds the first dorsal interosseous and, deeper, adductor pollicis; a needle passed straight through it reaches the palmar skin. The radial artery crosses the anatomical snuffbox and dives between the two heads of the first dorsal interosseous near the bases of the metacarpals. Dorsal branches of the superficial radial nerve and the dorsal venous network lie in the subcutaneous tissue; the dorsal branch of the ulnar nerve supplies the ulnar side. Between the metacarpals the dorsal interossei lie over the palmar interossei and, deeper, the flexor tendons, lumbricals and the common palmar digital vessels and nerves. On the fingers the skin and extensor expansion are thin over the phalanges and the interphalangeal joints; at the nail folds bone lies a few millimetres deep, with the digital nerves along the sides of the fingers.",
